From Wikipedia:

<<<
Silviculture is the practice of controlling the growth, composition/structure, as well as quality of forests to meet values and needs, specifically timber production. The name comes from the Latin silvi- ('forest') and culture ('growing'). Silviculture also focuses on making sure that the treatment(s) of forest stands are used to conserve and improve their productivity.
<<<
